1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:04,900
Ek waqt tha… jab Kingfisher sirf ek airline nahi, balki luxury ki pehchaan thi.

2
00:00:05,150 --> 00:00:09,900
2005 mein, Kingfisher Airlines ne Indian skies mein ek naya dream lekar entry ki.

3
00:00:10,150 --> 00:00:14,900
Premium seats, stylish cabin crew aur royal hospitality… flying ka experience hi badal gaya.

4
00:00:15,150 --> 00:00:19,900
Lekin founder Vijay Mallya ka vision sirf luxury tak limited nahi tha.

5
00:00:20,150 --> 00:00:24,900
2007 mein, Air Deccan ke acquisition ke saath Kingfisher ka empire aur bada ho gaya.

6
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:29,900
Aircraft badhe, routes badhe… lekin expansion ke saath expenses bhi badhne lage.

7
00:00:30,150 --> 00:00:34,900
Karz badhta gaya, financial pressure badhta gaya… aur situation mushkil hoti gayi.

8
00:00:35,150 --> 00:00:39,900
Salaries delay hone lagi, flights cancel hone lagi… aur passengers ka bharosa tootne laga.

9
00:00:40,150 --> 00:00:44,900
Phir aaya 20 October 2012… DGCA ne Kingfisher ka flying permit suspend kar diya.

10
00:00:45,150 --> 00:00:49,900
Jo airline kabhi aasman mein apni shaan dikhati thi… uske aircraft ab zameen par khade the.

11
00:00:50,150 --> 00:00:54,900
December 2012 ke end tak, Kingfisher ka flying licence bhi expire ho gaya… aur kabhi renew nahi hua.

12
00:00:55,150 --> 00:00:59,900
Ek glamorous airline… jo kabhi success ki misaal thi, ab business failure ki kahaani ban chuki thi.

13
00:01:00,150 --> 00:01:04,900
Lekin is poori kahaani se sabse bada lesson kya milta hai?

14
00:01:05,150 --> 00:01:09,900
Sirf bade sapne dekhna kaafi nahi… growth ke saath financial discipline bhi zaroori hai.

15
00:01:10,150 --> 00:01:14,900
Kyunki empire banana mushkil hai… lekin use tikaye rakhna usse bhi zyada mushkil.
